:- module(wildcard_goal, [go/2, f/1, chk/1, out/1, gather/1]).

:- chr_constraint go/2, f/1, chk/1, out/1, gather/1.

% An anonymous `_` handed to a named head variable must be a fresh
% logical variable, exactly like `_X` or `Y`. `f(X)` is told while `X` is
% still unbound, so `r`'s guard cannot decide yet and `f` is stored; the
% later `X = 1` has to reactivate it through the observer `f` registered
% on `X`. Written as `_` the value was the non-binding runtime wildcard:
% it registered no observer, `X = 1` was a silent no-op, and `f` stayed
% asleep, so `out(1)` was never told. The `named` case is the control,
% spelling the same thing with a name.
m @ go(X, R) <=> f(X), X = 1, gather(R).

% `r`'s guard delays on the unbound `N` and is retried only when the
% binding reactivates `f`, which is the path this directory pins.
r @ f(N) <=> N == 1 | chk(N).
c @ chk(1) <=> out(1).

g @ gather(R), out(V) <=> R = V.
